&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Radar helps businesses prevent fraud and abuse without getting in the way of legitimate customers. We combine machine learning powered by Stripe’s global network with intuitive dashboard experiences and developer APIs, to give our users comprehensive controls and insights to protect their business against threats ranging from payment fraud and card testing to bot and free trial abuse.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fraud doesn’t stand still, and it isn’t limited to checkout. As businesses launch new products and business models, attackers find new ways to exploit them. We obsess about understanding those attacks, identifying defenses that work, and making sophisticated fraud prevention simple for the businesses that depend on us to help them protect and grow their revenue with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a product manager on the Radar team, you’ll help customers, developers, and partners bring fraud prevention naturally into the systems and workflows they rely on. You’ll shape products that make fraud management feel effortless, connecting Radar’s capabilities to the tools and experiences our users build and run.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work at the intersection of customer needs and commercial opportunities to shape what we build and how we bring it to market. Working closely with engineering, data science, design, and go-to-market teams, you’ll build products and relationships that deliver lasting value to customers and partners. You’ll connect technical decisions to commercial outcomes while maintaining a high bar for reliability, craft, and the details that make complex products feel simple.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of the payments and fraud landscape, how businesses manage risk, and the systems and workflows they rely on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with customers, developers, and partners to uncover unmet needs, understand integration challenges, and identify opportunities to build broadly useful products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and communicate a clear product strategy and roadmap, prioritizing opportunities based on user impact, technical feasibility, and business value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with engineering and data science to turn sophisticated fraud control and monitoring capabilities into reliable APIs, intuitive tools, and well-crafted developer experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive product development from ideation through launch, setting the pace, scoping thoughtfully, prioritizing ruthlessly, and executing with rigor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate deeply with sales, marketing, and partnerships teams to identify opportunities, validate demand, and drive the adoption of new experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with customers and partners through early implementations, using hands-on feedback to improve documentation, onboarding, and the path from initial evaluation to production use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own metrics for integration success, adoption, retention, revenue, and user value; use results to guide product and commercial decisions and communicate progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly with internal and external stakeholders about priorities, trade-offs, progress, and results, building alignment across teams you don’t directly manage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of Product Management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly analytical, with a rigorous approach to quantitative and qualitative evidence. You’re comfortable digging into data, writing SQL when needed, and connecting product decisions to user and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scrappy and resourceful, with experience taking products from zero to one. You thrive in early-stage environments, test ideas quickly, and turn what you learn into products that scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial and business acumen. You understand how customer needs, market dynamics, and product differentiation translate into adoption and durable business value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven cross-functional leadership, including experience partnering with B2B sales teams on customer discovery, technical evaluation, and commercialization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping Dashboard and API products, with empathy for end users and developers alike.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing pricing and monetization models for B2B products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency to go deep with engineers on APIs, system architecture, and integration trade-offs, and to explain those decisions clearly to customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with a talent for distilling complex user problems into precise, actionable framing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ownership mindset and a high bar for product quality. You do what it takes to solve user problems and care deeply about the details of the experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building payments, fraud prevention, risk, or security products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building developer platforms and working with integration partners, including navigating technical dependencies and high-stakes external relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Stripe Security team is dedicated to improving the security of Stripe and its users. Our users trust us with some of their most sensitive information, and we make security a first-class consideration in everything we do. Security concerns are ever-evolving, creating an extremely dynamic environment for the Security team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Security Governance, Risk, and Compliance (SGRC) team helps Stripe make informed security decisions, understand its risk and control posture, and represent its security program to internal and external stakeholders. The team also manages security risk arising from Stripe’s relationships with third parties by assessing their security controls, identifying and mitigating risk, and supporting informed onboarding and risk-acceptance decisions. Our work helps Stripe move quickly while maintaining clear and consistent security expectations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently manage a portfolio of Third Party Security Risk Assessments (TPSRAs) for new engagements, renewals / reassessments, and material changes in relationship scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review security questionnaires, independent assurance reports, certifications, penetration-test results, and other evidence to evaluate third-party control effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify security gaps, determine proportionate remediation requirements, and clearly communicate findings to Stripe DRIs and cross-functional partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply Stripe’s third-party security standards consistently, documenting assessment results, decisions, and supporting evidence in Zip, Aravo, and other program systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate novel, complex, or high-risk findings and support Enhanced Due Diligence and risk-acceptance processes when a third party cannot meet Stripe’s security requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Procurement, Legal, Privacy, Business Continuity, Security, and business stakeholders to resolve assessment issues and support timely third-party onboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide practical guidance to Stripe teams on TPSRA requirements, timelines, and their responsibilities throughout the assessment process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track assessment volume, aging, service levels, remediation status, and other program-health indicators; use the data to identify trends and recommend improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify gaps in program processes, documentation, or tooling and contribute to implementing improvements that increase consistency, scalability, and stakeholder experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to third-party security risk policies, standards, procedures, and guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of relevant experience in third-party security risk, security assessments, information security, or a related risk-management function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting end-to-end third-party security assessments, including reviewing security documentation, identifying control gaps, determining risk, and defining remediation requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of common security and assurance frameworks, such as SOC 2, ISO 27001, PCI DSS, NIST, and CSA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment and analytical skills, including the ability to distinguish material security risks from lower-priority findings and recommend a proportionate response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to independently manage multiple assessments, priorities, and stakeholder relationships while meeting defined timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain technical security findings to non-security stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using operational data and reporting to identify trends, communicate program health, and improve processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative approach and experience working with cross-functional partners such as Procurement, Legal, Privacy, and business teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with third-party risk management platforms or procurement workflow tools such as Aravo, Zip, or similar systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Enhanced Due Diligence, security risk acceptance, or third-party incident response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience improving or scaling a third-party risk assessment program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trust is central to Stripe’s mission to grow the GDP of the internet and the Risk team advances that mission by building products and infrastructure that Stripe businesses, Stripe product teams, and Stripe’s network of regulators and financial partners rely on. From helping businesses onboard to Stripe to managing regulatory compliance at scale, Risk is at the center of what makes Stripe run. The Technical Program Manager team is responsible for delivering the cross-Stripe programs that help businesses grow on Stripe, enable products to launch safely at scale, and Stripe to maintain its position as the most trusted network in the financial ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead a team of TPMs and PGMs to deliver on Stripe’s most complex, cross-cutting, and critical programs. As a manager, you will support your team in leading programs that advance Stripe and Risk’s mission. You’ll hire, coach, and grow a team of excellent TPMs that support Stripe’s growing needs and the individuals’ careers. You will also act as a TPM yourself on the most complex initiatives that uniquely need your hands-on leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, lead and manage high-performing teams, managers, and individuals, across multiple locations, including providing performance reviews, continual feedback, and career growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and deliver on long-term vision and multi-year strategy for company-wide programs collaborating with product management and engineering leadership/executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define success criteria, delivery plans, track risks, and ensure successful execution of Risk’s most complex programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make substantial improvements to how the teams you work with communicate and operate to significantly increase the productivity and efficiency of the teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of management experience of varying seniority, including managing managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of software engineering, systems engineering or technical product/program management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience in finding and growing talent through coaching, mentoring, and career development conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving technical programs from ideation to delivery at scale and leading teams of Technical Program Managers who have done the same&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating autonomously and leading across multiple teams, with stakeholders in different disciplines across time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to demonstrate critical thinking and thought leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable working with geographically distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve managed teams that designed and operated critical infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are empathetic to customer needs but visionary enough to not just deliver a faster horse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are excited about collaborating with teammates across Stripe’s organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Past experience as an engineer or similar technical role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Radar helps businesses prevent fraud and abuse without getting in the way of legitimate customers. We combine machine learning powered by Stripe’s global network with intuitive dashboard experiences and developer APIs, to give our users comprehensive controls and insights to protect their business against threats ranging from payment fraud and card testing to bot and free trial abuse.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fraud doesn’t stand still, and it isn’t limited to checkout. As businesses launch new products and business models, attackers find new ways to exploit them. We obsess about understanding those attacks, identifying defenses that work, and making sophisticated fraud prevention simple for the businesses that depend on us to help them protect and grow their revenue with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a product manager on the Radar team, you’ll work directly with customers to understand the novel fraud and abuse attacks they face, identify the most important problems to solve, and turn those insights into product strategy and a roadmap.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work at the intersection of customers, engineering, data science, design, and commercial teams to shape what we build and bring it to market. Your work will span the fraud and abuse detection and control capabilities at the heart of Radar and the user and developer experiences that put those capabilities into our customers’ hands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires both urgency and taste. You’ll move quickly as threats evolve, without compromising on reliability, craft, or the details that make complex products feel beautifully simple.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of the fraud and abuse landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate emerging attacks with customers, assess their financial and operational impact, and distinguish isolated incidents from opportunities to build broadly useful defenses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate findings into a product strategy and roadmap, prioritizing the defenses that deliver the greatest customer and business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering, data science, and design to explore signals, shape solutions, and rapidly turn effective defenses into scalable, reliable products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the pace for the team by scoping the product thoughtfully, prioritizing ruthlessly, and executing with high rigor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with sales, marketing, and customer-facing teams to validate demand, coordinate launches, and help customers adopt and maximize the value they get from new capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own product performance, user experience, and business metrics to guide iteration and communicate progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of Product Management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly analytical, with a rigorous approach to quantitative and qualitative evidence. You’re comfortable digging into data, writing SQL when needed, and defining metrics that connect product decisions to user outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scrappy and resourceful, with experience taking products from zero to one. You find ways to test ideas quickly, learn from real users, and turn early solutions into products that scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial and business acumen. You understand how customer problems translate into willingness to pay, adoption, and durable business value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven cross-functional leadership, including experience partnering with B2B sales teams on customer discovery, product positioning, and adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping Dashboard and API products, with empathy for both end users and developers and an understanding of their different workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with substantial ambiguity. You can set direction with incomplete information, make thoughtful trade-offs, and adapt as new evidence emerges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency to go deep with engineering and data teams on complex systems, understand constraints, and evaluate alternative approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with a talent for distilling complex customer problems into precise, actionable framing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ownership mindset and a high bar for product quality. You do what it takes to solve user problems and care deeply about the details of the experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building fraud, abuse prevention, risk, or security products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing machine learning powered products and evaluating trade-offs between detection effectiveness and customer friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building tools for fraud analysts or risk teams, or developer products that support real-time decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software engineering, data science, or similar technical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Us&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Cloudflare, we are on a mission to help build a better Internet. Today the company runs one of the world’s largest networks that powers millions of websites and other Internet properties for customers ranging from individual bloggers to SMBs to Fortune 500 companies. Cloudflare protects and accelerates any Internet application online without adding hardware, installing software, or changing a line of code. Internet properties powered by Cloudflare all have web traffic routed through its intelligent global network, which gets smarter with every request. As a result, they see significant improvement in performance and a decrease in spam and other attacks. Cloudflare was named to Entrepreneur Magazine’s Top Company Cultures list and ranked among the World’s Most Innovative Companies by Fast Company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Cloudflare, we’re not looking for people who wait for a polished roadmap; we’re looking for the builders who see the cracks in the Internet that everyone else has simply learned to live with. We value candidates who have the instinct to spot a &quot;normalized&quot; problem and the AI-native curiosity to create a solution using the latest tools. Our culture is built on iteration, leveraging AI to ship faster today to make it better tomorrow, while ensuring that every improvement, no matter how small, is shared across the team to lift everyone up. If you’re the type of person who values curiosity over bureaucracy, and that AI is a partner in solving tough problems to keep the Internet moving forward, you’ll fit right in.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Manager at Cloudflare, you will be responsible for building products that improve the way that the Internet works. Product Managers at Cloudflare shape high-level product goals but also get our hands dirty. On an average day, you might pitch a concept to senior leadership, collaborate with marketing, work with designers to conduct user research, prototype a new feature, iterate on a spec, analyze usage data, and pair with an engineer on implementation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a strategic and technical Senior Product Manager to lead the vision, strategy, and evolution of our Threat Intelligence portfolio. Your mission is to ensure Cloudflare’s security products and customers can identify, understand, and respond to emerging threats earlier and with greater confidence. You will own the end-to-end roadmap for the platforms, data, and workflows that transform Cloudflare’s unique network signals and security research into timely, actionable intelligence, balancing speed and coverage with accuracy, context, and low false-positive rates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will translate a rapidly evolving threat landscape, from emerging attacker infrastructure and campaigns to new tactics, techniques, and procedures, into scalable capabilities that improve detection and response across Cloudflare’s security portfolio. You will serve as a bridge between threat researchers, intelligence analysts, engineering teams, and market-facing functions, working closely with Sales, Customer Success, and our customers to understand their challenges and drive adoption. Your success will be measured by the quality, timeliness, and actionability of our intelligence and its impact on customer security outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own your space. You will own the priorities and scope for a high performing engineering team focusing on detecting advanced threat actors.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect the pieces. Product managers are a nerve center at Cloudflare, responsible for connecting engineering, program management, marketing, revenue, and partners to make sure that our ships go out on time and with the maximum impact.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excel across teams. Enterprise capabilities cut across all of our product verticals, so you should be comfortable working with product managers across the company to prioritize systemic improvements that our enterprise customers need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be customer obsessed. You will be responsible for directly engaging with customers and understanding how they use our products. You’ll bring these insights back to the team to build a great roadmap.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Join pre-sales and post-sales calls with customers, sales, support, etc., to assist with, and help understand all phases of the customer lifecycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be data driven. You should be comfortable working with data, and analyzing data to quantify the impact of problems and opportunities in your space.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Key qualifications and skills&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience as a product manager delivering solutions in the cloud at scale for a technical audience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer focus. At Cloudflare, we serve the needs of customers large and small, and our product managers need to be comfortable understanding how to design for enterprises without compromising the experience for individuals and small businesses.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Fluency: &lt;/strong&gt;Demonstrated experience using AI assistants, coding tools, and agentic workflows to accelerate product work. You should be comfortable in an AI-native environment where tools like OpenCode are standard infrastructure, not optional perks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder management. You should bring hands-on experience in managing complex escalations and leading high-profile engagements (such as Quarterly Business Reviews). This includes delivering product updates to executive stakeholders (both internal and external), maintaining proactive communication during incidents, setting clear and realistic expectations, and driving cross-functional initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Acumen. You must have the ability to grasp complex technical concepts and be able to effectively translate these complex ideas for customers through various channels, including calls, blog posts, and reports. You must be comfortable engaging in deep technical discussions with engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preferred: candidate with professional experience in threat intelligence, adversary tactics and common TI frameworks, and/or general intelligence requirements and prioritization concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Compensation may be adjusted depending on work location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;This role is eligible to participate in Cloudflare’s equity plan.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cloudflare offers a complete package of benefits and programs to support you and your family.&amp;nbsp; Our benefits programs can help you pay health care expenses, support caregiving, build capital for the future and make life a little easier and fun!&amp;nbsp; The below is a description of our benefits for employees in the United States, and benefits may vary for employees based outside the U.S.&lt;/p&gt;
